{"seed":{"mim":"621730","entry_type":"phenotype","prefix":"#","title":"OOCYTE/ZYGOTE/EMBRYO MATURATION ARREST 28","alt_titles":[],"symbol":"OZEMA28","gene_symbols":[],"seed_pmids":[],"max_year":2025},"nodes":[{"id":"entry","type":"Entry","label":"OOCYTE/ZYGOTE/EMBRYO MATURATION ARREST 28","mim":"621730","entry_type":"phenotype"},{"id":"section:description","type":"Section","label":"description"},{"id":"section:nomenclature","type":"Section","label":"nomenclature"},{"id":"section:cloning_expression","type":"Section","label":"cloning_expression"},{"id":"section:gene_structure","type":"Section","label":"gene_structure"},{"id":"section:clinical_features","type":"Section","label":"clinical_features"},{"id":"section:other_features","type":"Section","label":"other_features"},{"id":"section:biochemical_features","type":"Section","label":"biochemical_features"},{"id":"section:inheritance","type":"Section","label":"inheritance"},{"id":"section:cytogenetics","type":"Section","label":"cytogenetics"},{"id":"section:mapping","type":"Section","label":"mapping"},{"id":"section:heterogeneity","type":"Section","label":"heterogeneity"},{"id":"section:gene_function","type":"Section","label":"gene_function"},{"id":"section:molecular_genetics","type":"Section","label":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"section:genotype_phenotype_correlations","type":"Section","label":"genotype_phenotype_correlations"},{"id":"section:pathogenesis","type":"Section","label":"pathogenesis"},{"id":"section:diagnosis","type":"Section","label":"diagnosis"},{"id":"section:clinical_management","type":"Section","label":"clinical_management"},{"id":"section:population_genetics","type":"Section","label":"population_genetics"},{"id":"section:evolution","type":"Section","label":"evolution"},{"id":"section:animal_model","type":"Section","label":"animal_model"},{"id":"section:history","type":"Section","label":"history"},{"id":"paper:40238067","type":"Paper","label":"Cui et al. (2025)","pmid":"40238067","year":2025,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Infertile females with biallelic mutations in APC/C genes are characterized by oocyte or early embryo defects."},{"id":"paper:37768355","type":"Paper","label":"Fan et al. (2023)","pmid":"37768355","year":2023,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Homozygous variants in CDC23 cause female infertility characterized by oocyte maturation defects."},{"id":"finding:37768355:1","type":"Finding","label":"Fan et al. (2023) described 3 infertile women with female infertility characterized by oocyte maturation defects.","pmid":"37768355","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"gene:CDC23","type":"Gene","label":"CDC23"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0008222","type":"Phenotype","label":"Female infertility","hpo_id":"HP:0008222"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0034914","type":"Phenotype","label":"Oocyte maturation arrest","hpo_id":"HP:0034914"},{"id":"inh:AR","type":"Inheritance","label":"Autosomal recessive","hpo_id":"HP:0000007"},{"id":"finding:37768355:2","type":"Finding","label":"In 3 infertile women with oocyte maturation defects, Fan et al. (2023) identified homozygous missense variants in the CDC23 gene, a core subunit of the anaphase-promoting complex/cyclosome (APC/C). One variant was c.986A-G (p.Tyr329Cys). In vitro experiments showed that this variant led to a decrease in CDC23 protein level.","pmid":"37768355","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"variant:CDC23:c.986A>G","type":"Variant","label":"CDC23 c.986A>G / p.Y329C","gene":"CDC23","keys":["c.986A>G","p.Y329C"],"omim_name":"CDC23, TYR329CYS"},{"id":"finding:37768355:3","type":"Finding","label":"Fan et al. (2023) identified a homozygous c.988C-T (p.Arg330Cys) missense variant in the CDC23 gene in women with female infertility characterized by oocyte maturation defects. The variant changed the localization of CDC23 in HeLa cells and mouse oocytes.","pmid":"37768355","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"variant:CDC23:c.988C>T","type":"Variant","label":"CDC23 c.988C>T / p.R330C","gene":"CDC23","keys":["c.988C>T","p.R330C"],"omim_name":"CDC23, ARG330CYS"},{"id":"finding:37768355:4","type":"Finding","label":"Fan et al. (2023) found that Cdc23 Y329C/Y329C knockin mice mimicked the patients' phenotype. Their oocytes had low expression of CDC23 and APC4 and accumulated securin and cyclin B1. Treatment with AZ3146 rescued the phenotype.","pmid":"37768355","section":"animal_model"},{"id":"finding:40238067:1","type":"Finding","label":"Cui et al. (2025) performed whole-exome sequencing in infertile women from 639 unrelated Chinese families. They identified 3 probands carrying APC/C gene variants. The infertility in these families was characterized by disturbed oocyte maturation, fertilization failure, and arrest of early embryonic development.","pmid":"40238067","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"gene:ANAPC13","type":"Gene","label":"ANAPC13"},{"id":"phenotext:fertilization failure","type":"PhenotypeText","label":"fertilization failure"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0032479","type":"Phenotype","label":"Preimplantation lethality","hpo_id":"HP:0032479"},{"id":"finding:40238067:2","type":"Finding","label":"In 2 unrelated Chinese women with infertility (cases 1 and 2), Cui et al. (2025) identified compound heterozygous missense variants in the CDC23 gene: c.A1277G, c.A833G, c.C182T, and c.C301T. The variants were found by whole-exome sequencing and followed a recessive inheritance pattern. The affected residues were conserved across species, and prediction programs (MutationTaster, SIFT, PolyPhen-2) suggested the variants were deleterious. In vitro studies suggested that the CDC23 variants caused dysregulated protein expression.","pmid":"40238067","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"variant:CDC23:c.1277A>G","type":"Variant","label":"CDC23 c.1277A>G","gene":"CDC23","keys":["c.1277A>G"],"omim_name":"CDC23, 1277A-G"},{"id":"variant:CDC23:c.833A>G","type":"Variant","label":"CDC23 c.833A>G","gene":"CDC23","keys":["c.833A>G"],"omim_name":"CDC23, 833A-G"},{"id":"variant:CDC23:c.182C>T","type":"Variant","label":"CDC23 c.182C>T","gene":"CDC23","keys":["c.182C>T"],"omim_name":"CDC23, 182C-T"},{"id":"variant:CDC23:c.301C>T","type":"Variant","label":"CDC23 c.301C>T","gene":"CDC23","keys":["c.301C>T"],"omim_name":"CDC23, 301C-T"},{"id":"finding:40238067:3","type":"Finding","label":"In an infertile Chinese woman (case 3), Cui et al. (2025) identified compound heterozygous variants in the APC13 (ANAPC13) gene: c.C6A and c.116_126del. The variants were found by whole-exome sequencing and followed a recessive pattern. In vitro studies suggested that the APC13 missense variant caused abnormal cellular localization of the protein. Structural modeling suggested that the APC/C variants may alter chemical bonds with other APC/C subunits.","pmid":"40238067","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"variant:ANAPC13:c.6C>A","type":"Variant","label":"ANAPC13 c.6C>A","gene":"ANAPC13","keys":["c.6C>A"],"omim_name":"ANAPC13, 6C-A"},{"id":"variant:ANAPC13:c.116_126del","type":"Variant","label":"ANAPC13 c.116_126del","gene":"ANAPC13","keys":["c.116_126del"],"omim_name":"ANAPC13, 116_126DEL"}],"edges":[{"src":"paper:37768355","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:37768355:1"},{"src":"finding:37768355:1","rel":"in_section","dst":"section:clinical_features"},{"src":"finding:37768355:1","rel":"mentions_gene","dst":"gene:CDC23","pmid":"37768355"},{"src":"finding:37768355:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0008222","pmid":"37768355","present":true,"frequency":"3/3","text":"female infertility"},{"src":"finding:37768355:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0034914","pmid":"37768355","present":true,"frequency":"3/3","text":"oocyte maturation defects"},{"src":"finding:37768355:1","rel":"asserts_inheritance","dst":"inh:AR","pmid":"37768355"},{"src":"paper:37768355","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:37768355:2"},{"src":"finding:37768355:2","rel":"in_section","dst":"section:molecular_genetics"},{"src":"finding:37768355:2","rel":"mentions_gene","dst":"gene:CDC23","pmid":"377683